SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0+
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: max17042: fix r0q 2 mOhm sense resistor, supplied status & VALRT IRQ storm

Fix three hardware/firmware interaction bugs on the Samsung Galaxy S22
(sm8450-samsung-r0q) MAX77705 fuel gauge (MAX17047-class at I2C 0x36):

1. Sense resistor scaling (2.5x capacity/current under-reporting):
   Samsung's OEM DT (r0q/max77705_fuelgauge.dtsi) sets
   `fuelgauge,fg_resistor = <5>; /* 2 milliohm */`, where enum 5 encodes
   2000 uOhm (2 mOhm), not 5000 uOhm. Override 5000 -> 2000 uOhm on
   `samsung,r0q` so `charge_full` / `charge_now` / `current_now` report the
   true 3,370 mAh (11.29 Wh) capacity and true charge/discharge current
   even when booted with an older DTB.

2. Prevent false DISCHARGING status & upowerd PowerOff bootloops while USB
   power is online:
   During cold-boot CPU + Wi-Fi initialization (~4.3 W transient load),
   instantaneous `MAX17042_Current` can briefly dip <= 0 even while VBUS is
   online (`power_supply_am_i_supplied > 0`). Check `MAX17042_AvgCurrent`
   first (`> 0` -> `CHARGING`, `<= 0` -> `NOT_CHARGING`) instead of reporting
   `DISCHARGING`, preventing `upowerd` from triggering an immediate critical
   battery `PowerOff` reboot loop when booting at low SOC on external power.

3. Disarm stale vendor `MAX17042_VALRT_Th` voltage alert thresholds:
   When `enable_por_init` is false and DT leaves `vmin`/`vmax` unset, stale
   bootloader `VALRT_Th` thresholds cause a continuous ~5.7 Hz threaded IRQ
   wakeup storm (>1,000 wakeups) whenever `VCELL` sits below the vendor
   alert floor. Reset `MAX17042_VALRT_Th` to `0xff00` at probe and if
   `STATUS_VMN_BIT | STATUS_VMX_BIT` fires without DT thresholds.

Credits:
- MyungJoo Ham / Samsung Electronics (upstream GPL-2.0+ max17042_battery.c
  and SM-S901E GPL-2.0 max77705_fuelgauge sense-resistor reference).

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/max17042_battery.c b/drivers/power/supply/max17042_battery.c
index f4433c6..8fe1507 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/max17042_battery.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/max17042_battery.c
@@ -182,10 +182,24 @@ static int max17042_get_status(struct max17042_chip *chip, int *status)
 
 	current_now = sign_extend32(data, 15);
 
-	if (current_now > 0)
+	if (current_now > 0) {
+		*status = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_CHARGING;
+		return 0;
+	}
+
+	/*
+	 * While external power is online (am_i_supplied > 0), transient load
+	 * spikes (e.g. CPU/Wi-Fi init during boot) can momentarily exceed
+	 * input_current_limit and drive instantaneous Current <= 0. Check
+	 * AvgCurrent first; if still <= 0, report NOT_CHARGING rather than
+	 * DISCHARGING so userspace (upowerd) never mistakes a plugged-in load
+	 * spike at low SOC for an unplugged critical discharge.
+	 */
+	ret = regmap_read(chip->regmap, MAX17042_AvgCurrent, &data);
+	if (ret == 0 && sign_extend32(data, 15) > 0)
 		*status = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_CHARGING;
 	else
-		*status = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_DISCHARGING;
+		*status = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_NOT_CHARGING;
 
 	return 0;
 }
@@ -979,6 +993,15 @@ static irqreturn_t max17042_thread_handler(int id, void *dev)
 		max17042_enable_soc_alerts(chip);
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * Disarm stale bootloader/vendor voltage alert thresholds if DT did
+	 * not configure vmin/vmax, preventing a 5.7 Hz IRQ wakeup storm when
+	 * VCELL sits below a leftover vendor VEmpty threshold.
+	 */
+	if ((val & (STATUS_VMN_BIT | STATUS_VMX_BIT)) &&
+	    chip->vmin == INT_MIN && chip->vmax == INT_MAX)
+		regmap_write(chip->regmap, MAX17042_VALRT_Th, 0xff00);
+
 	/* we implicitly handle all alerts via power_supply_changed */
 	regmap_clear_bits(chip->regmap, MAX17042_STATUS,
 			  0xFFFF & ~(STATUS_POR_BIT | STATUS_BST_BIT));
@@ -1018,6 +1041,15 @@ static int max17042_parse_dt(struct max17042_chip *chip)
 	if ((of_property_read_u32(np, "shunt-resistor-micro-ohms",
 				  &prop) == 0) ||
 	    (of_property_read_u32(np, "maxim,rsns-microohm", &prop) == 0)) {
+		/*
+		 * Samsung Galaxy S22 (sm8450-samsung-r0q) uses a 2 mOhm
+		 * (2000 uOhm) sense resistor (vendor DT fuelgauge,fg_resistor = <5>,
+		 * where 2 = 5 mOhm and 5 = 2 mOhm). Override DTs that encoded
+		 * <5> as 5000 uOhm so capacity (3370 mAh) and current are not
+		 * under-reported by 2.5x.
+		 */
+		if (prop == 5000 && of_machine_is_compatible("samsung,r0q"))
+			prop = 2000;
 		chip->r_sns = prop;
 		chip->enable_current_sense = true;
 	}
@@ -1226,6 +1258,9 @@ static int max17042_probe(struct i2c_client *client, struct device *dev, int irq
 						chip->battery->desc->name,
 						chip);
 		if (!ret) {
+			if (!chip->enable_por_init &&
+			    chip->vmin == INT_MIN && chip->vmax == INT_MAX)
+				regmap_write(chip->regmap, MAX17042_VALRT_Th, 0xff00);
 			regmap_update_bits(chip->regmap, MAX17042_CONFIG,
 					CFG_ALRT_BIT_ENBL,
 					CFG_ALRT_BIT_ENBL);
